From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] display/samsung: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(display/samsung: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/display/samsung to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - platform_driver.remove returns void (6.11)
  - strlcpy() removed, use strscpy() (6.8)
  - of_property_for_each_u32() takes 3 arguments (6.11)
  - MODULE_IMPORT_NS() takes a string literal (6.13)
  - <asm/unaligned.h> moved to <linux/unaligned.h> (6.12)
  - iommu_register_device_fault_handler() removed (6.8): use the pixel_iommu fault registry that samsung_iommu.ko exports
  - DRM: fb_create() takes the format info, get_format_info(u32, u64) (6.17)
  - DRM: drm_dbg_printer(), struct_mutex and drm_driver.date removed
  - drm_info()/drm_warn() now require a real struct drm_device
  - panel: drm_bridge attach takes the encoder; atomic_* callbacks take drm_atomic_state (6.16)
  - panel: include <linux/debugfs.h> explicitly

Files: dp_audio/dp_dma.c, exynos_drm_debug.c, exynos_drm_decon.c, exynos_drm_dp.c, exynos_drm_dpp.c, exynos_drm_drv.c, exynos_drm_dsim.c, exynos_drm_fb.c, exynos_drm_gem.c, exynos_drm_tui.c, exynos_drm_writeback.c, panel/panel-samsung-drv.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * struct drm_atomic_state -> struct drm_atomic_commit (upstream
    5164f7e7ff8e, applied with the same sed).
  * atomic_reset/drm_atomic_helper_bridge_reset -> atomic_create_state/
    drm_atomic_helper_bridge_create_state.
  * dma_fence::lock is accessed through dma_fence_spinlock() /
    dma_fence_{lock_irqsave,unlock_irqrestore}() now.
  * panel/panel-samsung-drv.c: drm_panel_init() is static; same
    jy_drm_panel_init() as display/common's gs_panel (see there).
    FB_BLANK_* needs <linux/fb.h>.
  * dp_audio/dp_dma.c: RESERVEDMEM_OF_DECLARE() takes a reserved_mem_ops
    table; node_init gets the fdt node.
  * mechanical of_node_to_fwnode()/irq_domain_add_*() conversions.

lynx-linus-mainline (android-mainline -> Linus' v7.3; ACK-only interfaces are
handled here rather than restored in the kernel, see kernel/patches/README.md):
  * exynos_drm_gem: allocate from the "system" heap with samsung_dma_heap_find()/
    samsung_dma_heap_buffer_alloc() instead of ACK's dma_heap_find() & co.
  * exynos_drm_decon, panel: sched_setscheduler[_nocheck]() via
    <soc/google/sched-setscheduler.h>; panel: drm_mode_convert_to_umode()
    copied locally.
  * exynos_drm_dp, exynos_drm_debug: strncpy() from <soc/google/linus-compat.h>.
